{"title":"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>One commercially available ten-button lock may be opened by pressing -- in any order -- the correct five buttons. The sample shown below has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed33219f42317851baeedac0634c5d57d09220bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,3,6,9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> as its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Combination\" title=\"Combination\">combination</a>. Suppose that these locks are redesigned so that sets of as many as nine buttons or as few as one button could serve as combinations. How many additional combinations would this allow?\n</p>\n<center><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:1988-1.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/89/1988-1.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"191\" height=\"146\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Currently there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79aa77ebe8a84b8bb55ef96cb307fec092f5a438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${10 \\choose 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\" /> possible combinations.\nWith any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the number of ways to choose a set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> buttons is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296bb8abdaef1ee86c79a743353c26e65d975fd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum^{9}_{k=1}{10 \\choose k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"71\" height=\"53\" />.\nNow we can use the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c68c0a4bca9f93e22604b02e04874040781526a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum^{n}_{k=0}{n \\choose k}=2^{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"109\" height=\"53\" />.\nSo the number of additional combinations is just\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/7/617285f1325d49f2cdd792e0b90619a5dc1b56d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{10}-{10\\choose 0}-{10\\choose 10}-{10 \\choose 5}=1024-1-1-252=\\boxed{770}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"464\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nNote: A simpler way of thinking to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b2422eb1e019642032c00b0c5d5982903fe45d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> is thinking that each button has two choices, to be black or\n</p><p>to be white.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME\" title=\"1988 AIME\">1988 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1988 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1988\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017180745\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications